hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-5 : List (List Word)
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-5 = cons "**Abstract.** A knowledge graph is supposed to represent what is known so that it can be shared, combined," (cons "queried and extended. The technologies built for this over the past twenty-five years all represent assertions." (cons "None of them represents knowing. An edge says that a relation holds, but it doesn't contain the reason it holds." (cons "Two identifiers are declared to name the same thing without saying what carries over between them. Inference" (cons "runs outside the graph, and its results go stale silently. Hyperactivity starts from a different object: a" (cons "construction, which is code with a type together with the rationale that establishes it, kept in a store" (cons "addressed by content. From that one choice, the problems knowledge-graph research treats as separate (identity," (cons "provenance, uncertainty, schema evolution, integration, inference and maintenance) each become a property of a" (cons "single construction. This is a universal theory of knowledge graphs in a precise sense: any graph in today's" (cons "formats can be represented in it without loss, and none of today's formats can represent what it adds." (cons "" nil))))))))))
